```
function merge_sort(list):
    if length of list <= 1:
        return list

    middle = length of list // 2
    left = merge_sort(list[0:middle])
    right = merge_sort(list[middle:])

    return merge(left, right)

function merge(left, right):
    result = empty list
    while left is not empty and right is not empty:
        if left[0] <= right[0]:
            append left[0] to result
            remove left[0] from left
        else:
            append right[0] to result
            remove right[0] from right

    append any remaining elements of left to result
    append any remaining elements of right to result

    return result
```
This recursively splits the list, sorts each half, and merges them back together.

